asl-parrot (1.7-1) UNRELEASED; urgency=low

  * Various performance optimizations in amp-core.
  * Added daemon-reload to postint [Issue 1](https://github.com/Ampersand-ASL/asl-parrot/issues/1).

asl-parrot (1.6-1) UNRELEASED; urgency=low

  * Per Jason N8EI, split the initial greeting into two parts to reduce
  conflict with telemetry announcements.
  * Tweaked coefficients of FIR filters to improve audio quality.
  * Incorporated support for Talker ID telemetry messages.
  * Added a farewell message when dropping line.
  * Moved files from /usr/etc to /etc.
  
 -- Bruce MacKinnon <bruce@mackinnon.com>  Tue, 05 Feb 2026 14:00:00 -0500

asl-parrot (1.5-1) UNRELEASED; urgency=low

  * Added a subjective assessment in "layperson's language" for 
  the audio level. Pay close attention to etc/asl-parrot.env because
  there are some new environment variables needed to make this work.
  * Cleared up some problems with timed out connections.
  * Added source address and version to the /network-test API endpoint.
      
 -- Bruce MacKinnon <bruce@mackinnon.com>  Tue, 20 Jan 2026 14:00:00 -0500

asl-parrot (1.4-1) UNRELEASED; urgency=low

  * Added network test with voice prompt. The parrot will "call back" using
  the registered address/port of your node to see if a connection is 
  possible. This is done using the POKE/PONG feature of the IAX protocol.
  * Added an HTTP endpoint to support an IAX ping on an arbitrary node. Use
  http://asl-parrot:8080/network-test?node=xxxxx.
      
 -- Bruce MacKinnon <bruce@mackinnon.com>  Tue, 20 Jan 2026 14:00:00 -0500

